{"kind":"artifact","text":"The fold projects the satisfier it bound at admission, and the profile advances to workroom-fold@14 because main took @13 first. Exact clean pushed head e1798050b37e8a3c48f985a672afc1628beff9a2 on request/decision-records-ui-v3; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash 487c41a9, checkout clean. Filed under planner's b03f55fe as amended by e6e158a8, on my promise 746388e3.\n\nWHAT THIS PATH CHANGES. fold.go projects a Satisfier per statement from the definition captured on the record at admission, so a reader can tell who may ratify without replaying every kind definition in reading order. decideRatify reads the same captured definition, so the projection publishes exactly what the fold decides on. An empty satisfier means the fold bound no definition and nothing may be ratified on it. The two goldens take insertion-only additions.\n\nTHE PROFILE COLLISION, WHICH IS THE ONE DELIBERATE DEVIATION FROM A PURE CARRY. This lane bumped workroom-fold@12 to @13. While it was blocked, main independently bumped @12 to @13 for the guarded unclaimed-reassignment work at 4784ab98. Two different projection changes claimed the same version. I verified this at four commits rather than inferring it: schema.go reads @12 at d8edc000 and at 1eeae934, and @13 at both 02558e8d (main) and 18a6ea29 (this lane's abandoned predecessor). This head therefore advances to workroom-fold@14.\n\nWHY THAT IS NOT COSMETIC. Reusing @13 would let a cache written by main's shipped @13 binary — which carries no Satisfier — pass the version gate. Every reader served from that cache would be told there is no satisfier, and every ratification would be silently withheld from actors entitled to make it. That is precisely the defect this lane exists to close, reintroduced by a version number that failed to distinguish two changes. The bump is forced, not chosen.\n\nCONSEQUENCES CARRIED THROUGH. The cache witness in internal/app moves from @12-to-@13 to @13-to-@14. docs/reference/architecture.md line 815 states @14 for this projection change; line 701 still states @13 for main's, which is historically accurate and left alone. Main's own test stays seeded at @12 — a fold that genuinely lacks the guarded schemas — with only its expected value moved to @14.\n\nMAIN'S WORK SURVIVES THE CARRY. I checked rather than assumed: the guarded-retirement and reassignment symbols are present at this head in fold.go, reassign_if_unclaimed_test.go and schema.go, the same three files that carry them at main. No file main has is deleted by this head except the two superseded uidist bundle assets, which the rebuild replaces.\n\nGATES RUN BY ME AT THIS EXACT HEAD, from a run I watched exit, not taken from the agent that performed the carry. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok plus 1 no-test-files, zero failures and zero cached; gofmt -l . empty; go build ./... and go vet ./... exit 0 with no output; npm test --prefix ui 99 tests, 99 pass, 0 fail; make ui exit 0 leaving git status empty, so internal/service/uidist is byte-reproduced; make ui-check exit 0; git diff --check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"e1798050b37e8a3c48f985a672afc1628beff9a2","path":"internal/workroom"}}